{'base__uid': 793, 'base__ref_base': '-', 'base__alt_base': 'A', 'base__hugo': 'ISG15', 'base__cchange': 'c.-108+914_-108+915insA', 'base__so': 'INT', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs201014604', 'gnomad__af': 0.07823195144, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'hom', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'The protein encoded by this gene is a ubiquitin-like protein that is conjugated to intracellular target proteins upon activation by interferon-alpha and interferon-beta. Several functions have been ascribed to the encoded protein, including chemotactic activity towards neutrophils, direction of ligated target proteins to intermediate filaments, cell-to-cell signaling, and antiviral activity during viral infections. While conjugates of this protein have been found to be noncovalently attached to intermediate filaments, this protein is sometimes secreted. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2012]'}
