{'base__uid': 1064, 'base__ref_base': 'T', 'base__alt_base': 'C', 'base__hugo': 'TNFRSF18', 'base__cchange': 'c.*1387A>G', 'base__so': '2KD', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs367865534', 'gnomad__af': 0.0179916317992, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'This gene encodes a member of the TNF-receptor superfamily. The encoded receptor has been shown to have increased expression upon T-cell activation, and it is thought to play a key role in dominant immunological self-tolerance maintained by CD25(+)CD4(+) regulatory T cells. Knockout studies in mice also suggest the role of this receptor is in the regulation of CD3-driven T-cell activation and programmed cell death. Three alternatively spliced transcript variants of this gene encoding distinct isoforms have been reported. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2011]'}
