{'base__uid': 1560, 'base__ref_base': 'T', 'base__alt_base': 'C', 'base__hugo': 'CDK11B', 'base__cchange': 'c.*221A>G', 'base__so': 'UT3', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs1435930760', 'gnomad__af': None, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'hom', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'This gene encodes a member of the serine/threonine protein kinase family. Members of this kinase family are known to be essential for eukaryotic cell cycle control. Due to a segmental duplication, this gene shares very high sequence identity with a neighboring gene. These two genes are frequently deleted or altered in neuroblastoma. The protein kinase encoded by this gene can be cleaved by caspases and may play a role in cell apoptosis. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Apr 2014]'}
